Hello Mark!


> Is it safe to remove the "Load Board" and plug other things in?  There
> is enough room in that box to hold a couple more disk drives and the
> Exabyte.

Normally the load board is in there because of the TK50. When idle the
TK50 consumes very little current from the power supply and because
switching power supplies demand a minimal load and the TK50 doesn't
consume enough power when idle they put in a minimal load for the power
supply. If you put in an Exabyte I would suggest leaving the board inside,
if you put in a harddisk  next to an Exabyte for example you can leave out
the load board.

> Does anyone know the capacity of the power supply in this thing?

I think most of them are around 65 Watts (there are three different types
though!) and they supply 3 Amps on +5 and +12 Volts maximum.

Greetings, Jeffrey Willemsen




