>         :if=/usr/lbin/hplaser4psof:\
>         :lf=/usr/adm/lp1err:\
>         :lp=@hplasertest\hplaser:\
>         :mx#0:\
>         :of=/usr/lbin/hplaser4psof:\
>         :pl#66:\
>         :pw#80:\
>         :rw:\
>         :sd=/usr/spool/lpd1:\
>         :xf=/usr/lbin/xf:
> 

For lp1  you also need a line in your /etc/services file like:

hplaser		9100/tcp

The Apple is possibly using some weird port of its own and
you will need to redo its entry to match lp1's setup but with
its own port entry in /etc/services. Another possibility is 
that the queue name "text" is wrong.

The problem with lp0 is possibly a mismatch between the parallel
port setting (eg EPP/ECP/etc) that the printer expects and that 
the system is setup for. You need to look for your system manual
and lookup how to change that. On some machines you might need 
to switch from SRM console to ARC console and then run isacfg.

YMMV

Charlie

