Mark,

The RDxx and TK50 expansion boxes, Decmate III and Vaxstation 2000 all
use a variant of the box and power supply - the load board is to ensure
a minimum load on the 5 volt rail so that the regulation of the 12v and
other rails stay within spec. This is sensed via the 5v rail only and if
there isn't enough load @ 5volts, other voltages will tend to drop a
little.

That's the theory - in practice, you can safely take out the load board
if you have a wini or two inside the box - an amp or so at 12/5 volts
seems to run fine.

Rgrds, Chris 

