  The main cause of failure seems to be a supply that had been sitting for
an extended period without being used (like in a used equipment vendor's
warehouse 8-).

  Most of the problem supplies seem to have been on RD-series disks, but I
did have 2 LEP TK50 boxes that had failed supplies.

  Note that we may well be talking about two different types of enclosure.
I am referring to the LEP (Low End Peripheral/Leprechaun) enclosure which
was used for the RD5x and TK50 devices. It's deeper (front-to-back) than
it is wide, and uses the same "skid plate" as the BA23/BA123 for mounting
its drive.

  There is another type of expansion box which is about the same size as
a VAXstation 2000 (wider than it is deep) which was used for SCSI periph-
erals like the RZxx disks and the TK50-GZ SCSI tape. It has a handle on
the back (which seems to be designed to interfere with the SCSI connectors
also on the back 8-) That is *not* the box I'm talking about.

