I have two LEP enclosures, and the power supplies failed on BOTH of them
(with RD52s inside).  I phoned the supply manufacturer, and they wanted
$150 for repair, or $350 for a new supply.  This seemed excessive, since
the empirical failure rate of 100% implied the supply was under-specified
or had a design flaw (RD drives do tend to get "hungrier" with age).

I ended up modifying the wiring harness and substituting a nice unit from
Power General (about $100).

