In article <362CFA23.200E@sen.ca.gov>, David Spencer <David.Spencer@sen.ca.gov> writes:
:Yep, I was having a little too much fun switching back and forth between
:the SRM and ARC consoles on my AlphaStation 200 4/166. Now the machine
:is completely unresponsive when I turn it on. I'm sure I'm not the first
:person to do this - does any one know the secret to resetting or
:otherwise restoring the EPROM so I can use my machine again?

  Look around under:

    ftp://ftp.digital.com/pub/DEC/Alpha/firmware/utilities/
    ftp://ftp.digital.com/pub/Digital/Alpha/firmware/readmes/alpha200.html

  Use the above to create yourself a failsafe loader floppy.  On the 
  AlphaStation 200, jumper J2 pin 1 to 2 (pin 2 to 3 is the normal 
  position, loading the firmware from FlashRAM) to invoke the failsafe 
  floppy loader when the system powers up.  The system will then load
  the necessary firmware off the floppy disk.

