At my company we are running a VAX 10000.  As part of a new hardware policy,
we are converting a bunch of DEC 90TL Terminal servers running DEC LM324
printers from the LAT proticol to TCP.	The problem is thus:  When we convert
the print queues on the VAX to TCP from LAT (lots of TLAs), we must also
change the setting in either the terminal server or the printer so that a
carrige return (CR) is replaced by a carriage return and a line feed (CR-LF).
 Without this change, the printer just prints the whole job on one line.

This hardware-level change also affects other jobs being sent to the printer
from other servers (SCO unix, NT, etc) that do not rely on the VAX queue.  Is
there a way to make this substitution (CR-LF for CR) in the TCP queue on the
VAX box instead of changing the printer or the terminal server?

Thanks,

Alexander Brewer, IE.

