From the Digital WEB site you can send a question to the WEBmaster and
question will get forwarded to someone in support that will attempt to
answer your question. There is also the Starion phone support at 800-554-3333.
This is a dedicated group that only supports Starion. The warranty on the
Starion 9xx was for 3 years - one year on-site and the 2nd and 3rd year
carry-in.
This also included 3 years for phone support. If you're still in the warranty
period, you should be able to call support.

Most of the normal questions can be found in the documentation - adding
extra disks, installing faster processors, etc.

The Starion 9xx series was designed to be industry compatible in the area of
motherboard form factor (the chassis is designed on a standard called
"Western Digital LPx" which calls out placement for motherboard mounting
screws, placement of the I/O connectors, etc). The memory system uses
standard 72-pin, 70ns SIMMs. The disks are EIDE.

The motherboard has jumpers (see Appendix A) that allow you to set the base
frequency for the CPU and clock multipliers (you can run an Intel Pentium from
75 to 133Mhz by changing the jumpers). You can also get something called the
"Evergreen" upgrade that I believe is an AMD K6 200 and up the performance.

The area that is not upgradeable is the L2 cache.

