Of course it works O,K, but you have another option.

Step 1.
>>> B -flag 0,1   ( Alpha )
>>> B/1           ( VAX )

Step 2.
SYSBOOT> SET SETTIME 1
SYSBOOT> CONT

Step 3.
The machine inquires current date and time.
You can answer the question at the console terminal.

Step 4.
After Step 3, it continues boot sequence as usual.

This means will trouble you more, but has less
influence on VMS and application programs.

