We have been having some problem running large jobs on an Alpha 255/233
workstation. Our code is written in Fortran 77, compiled with f77 and
it requires approximately 199 Mbytes of RAM.
When we attempt running this code on a machine with 512 MB of RAM, we 
get the following error message:

1594:str2: /sbin/loader: Fatal Error: set_program_attributes failed to set heap
start

This machine has Digital UNIX V4.0B. If we try running the very same code on
another Alpha 255/233, which has only 160 MB of RAM and an older version
of the operating system, Digital UNIX V3.2D-1, the code starts running
fine, except for the obvious problems due to the fact that it does not fit
in the physical memory.

A third test, performed on a machine with Digital UNIX V4.0B, but a memory
of only 128 MB, has led to the very same Fatal Error, therefore it seems to 
depend on the version of the operating system or on the default kernel 
configuration associated with a particular version of the operating system,
rather then on the actual memory size.

We have also tried compiling a static version of the code, with the option
-non_shared, and in this case we get the following error on all three 
machines:

Insufficent memory to open Fortran RTL message catalog, message #41.

Does anybody know what we can do to successfully run our code on the 
machine with 512 MB RAM?

