From: Alan Dartnell <Adartnel@esoc.esa.de>
Subject: Porting a macro-64 source from VMS to NT
Date: 1998/10/25
Message-ID: <36333215.6C2397A9@esoc.esa.de>#1/1
X-Deja-AN: 404852881
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 7bit
Organization: ESA/ESOC - European Space Operations Centre
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=us-ascii
Mime-Version: 1.0
Newsgroups: comp.sys.dec,comp.os.vms

I have been asked to look at the possibility of porting a large MACRO-64

application from VMS to an Alpha-NT system.

The application was originally written in MACRO-64 for performance
reasons,
the performance of a C version was measured as less than half as fast
as the MACRO-64 version and unable to provide the required performance.

It never looked like being an easy job, but on investigating the asaxp
assembler it looks to be much harder than was originally assumed.

There is no VMS system specific code other than the $Routine, $Return,
$Call macros, and these are readily replaced. All register are refered
to using symbolic names so there are no problems in accommodating the
different register usages of VMS and NT.

However it does make very heavy use of the MACRO-64's macro facilities
and of its string and integer symbol manipulation capabilities. These
seem to be almost nonexistent in the asaxp assembler which appears to
use the C preprocessor for these purposes, and this is simply not
capable
of performing the required macro and string processing.

Does any one know of any macro processor for alpha NT ? If not its looks

like the direct porting option will have to be abandoned.

We are also investigating other options, such as porting the output
produced by MACRO-64 using the /PREPROCESS_ONLY qualifier or using
a high level language to perform the macro task and have it generate
a simple assembler program.








