> but I don't have any experience on ULTRIX and a DECstation.

  The RRD42 was a Sony CDU-541 with modified firmware - if the 4th jumper 
position has a jumper, it reported an ID of "DEC RRD42" and had a 512-
byte blocksize. If the jumper was out, it behaved as a normal Sony. The
jumper was purple, in the IBM tradition.

  The RRD40 and RRD50 were LMS drives - the less said, the better.

  There wasn't an RRD41.

