In article <70qcf2$n50$1@nnrp1.dejanews.com>, rceci@adams.com writes:
:(2) as4100: each 2GB, 1 CIPCA, dual DE500, memory channel, OVMS 7.1-H1

  I will assume OpenVMS Alpha V7.1-1H1, as there is no "V7.1-H1" 
  release I am aware of...

  Abbreviating widget names can potentially lead to confusion among
  the readers, as there are a number of similar (but different) systems 
  -- these clearly appear to be AlphaServer 4100 series systems, but 
  which models -- and answers erroneous to your particular platform
  can potentially be posted.

:I believe I have the memory channel working correctly, but I am seeing
:some peculiar behavior when I either node boots or is otherwise removed
:from the cluster.  The other node hangs temporarily (30seconds - 1 minute),
:while the other node leaves the cluster and the cnxman makes a transition.

  Which specific memory channel hardware is in use here?

  Do you have a big lock tree?  (Large relational databases are one common
  source of a large lock resource tree, among the various applications that
  one commonly sees in configurations such as this.)

  What is RECNXINTERVAL set to?

  How far apart are the nodes physically located?  (Obviously 90 meters
  or less, if you have CI configured.)

  Exactly how are you removing the system?  Power-down or direct HALT
  is among the worst ways, because the other nodes must time out -- a 
  normal or even direct OPCCRASH shutdown will send out a "last gasp"
  transition", which will make for faster transitions.

  A quorum disk -- which another posting from you in this thread indicates 
  that you have configured here -- will also slow transitions.  Smaller
  values of QDSKINTERVAL (as low as 1, for instance) will also speed up
  transitions.  (Setting this value low does also reduce the ability of 
  the cluster to hit a network speed bump without disintegrating. :-)

  Are you using multihost SCSI?

  Are you using port allocation classes?  (Based on another posting,
  you are obviously using allocation classes.)

  Is the Alpha firmware current on both nodes?

:mc_cable/mc_diag all have passed.  mca0 shows unavailable (normal),
:and pma0 shows online, 1 or 2 errors.  sh cluster/cont with "add lport" and
:"add cable" shows cluster services connected across the MC.

  Have you applied the various recommended and mandatory ECO kits?
  Particularly have you applied the ALPMC ECO kit that is available 
  for the V7.1, V7.1-1H1, and V7.1-1H2 releases?

:This is a bit disconcerting.  The nodes are cabled point-to-point (vc0 and vc1
:respectively).  Would a hub help?

  Hubs are generally part of "larger" configurations.

  From another message of yours in this particular thread:

:Lost' messages on the system console also" ?  Come-on!  I have been building
:clusters for almost a decade. OK, just for grins, I checked:
:
:votes=1
:expected_votes=2
:disk_quorum="$1$DUA100"
:qdskvotes=1

  If *both* AlphaServer 4100 nodes have this same parameter configuration,
  then you have an erronous (and quite dangerous to the integrity of your 
  data and to your continued system operations) cluster configuration.  As 
  a result of this misconfiguration, your disk data is presently being 
  exposed to the possibility of severe corruptions.  Please see the OpenVMS 
  Frequently Asked Questions (FAQ) for details on the proper setting of the 
  system parameter EXPECTED_VOTES.  (If the nodes have different parameter
  settings, please post the parameter output from a SYSGEN SHOW/CLUSTER for 
  both AlphaServer 4100 nodes.)
 
 -------------------------- pure personal opinion ---------------------------
