We are running several dozen TCP/IP printers from Multinet on VMS.
What kind of problems are you having?

In general we:
1) Create the multinet NLP devices at VMS boot time using sysgen.
2) Assign the proper logical name to each nlp device.  I can send the
exact syntax from work.
3) HP JetDirect cards use port 9100 at their assigned IP address.
Our Windows NT admins run Jetadmin and assign a static IP to the card.
4) We assign a logical /sys/exec to associate the NLP device with the
IP/port
5) Create the queue on the nlp device.

Note: The HP JetDirect external boxes use ports 9100, 9101, etc...

