Terry probably has more experience with these boxes than I do,
so I don't want to seem to contradict him.  However, in the
past couple of years I've taken several old TK50 boxes and
replaced the tape drive and controller board with SCSI disk
drives, or even other kinds of tape drives.  So far they
all work.

I think that there is a reasonable chance that the bad power
supplies have all self-destructed by now, and that any boxes
that still work probably have good power supplies in them.

All that aside: if this is an important piece of equipment,
you may want to buy a better box to put it in.  The price of
external SCSI storage boxes seems to have come down a bit
in the last few years.

