Vince (AA9TL) wrote:

> I got a DEC LN03R Scriptprinter at an auction sans manual. Anybody out there
> know what error code 4 means? The little man (call maintanance) is also lit.

According to the Manual, there are 3 symbols on the indicator panel.
Paper Jam (PJ), Controller Error (CE) and Call Field Service (CFS) from
left to right.

Printer Errors:

Symbol	Error	Problem			
CFS	1	Fusing
CFS	2	Optical System
CFS	4	OPC Sync Mark
CFS	8	Main Motor
CFS	F	Engine Driver

The other error numbers are simply additions of the listed errors, e.g.
5 means error 4 and 1 occured.

Symbol	Error	Problem			
None	C	Cover open
PJ	E	Paper exit or fusing area jam
PJ	F	Paper feed jam

Controller Errors (CE symbol is on):

Error	Controller Status
31	Communication error on received character
32	Communication error input buffer overflow
53	Loop back test failure control bits
54	Loop back test failure transmit/receive test
56	Loop back test ok
71	ROM error
72	RAM error
7	Fatal controller error
6	Printer busy


In your case, I would change the OPC cartridge. You have to pull the
development drawer at the front of the printer, above the paper tray,
for access.

> Also could use info on the setting of the DIP switches in the back.

Switch Pack 1:

Switch	Setting	Parameter
1 -4 		Baud rate, see next table
5	Off	8 Data Bits *
	On	7 Data Bits
6	Off	Parity Disabled *
	On	Parity Enabled

Baud rate settings:

SP1-1	SP1-2	SP1-3	SP1-4	Baud rate
off	off	off	off	1200
off	off	off	on	2400
off	off	on	off	3600
off	off	on	on	4800
off	on	off	off	7200
off	on	off	on	9600 *
off	on	on	off	19200
off	on	on	on	38400
on	off	off	off	57600 (not yet implemented)

Switch Pack 2:

Switch	Setting	Parameter
1	off	Even Parity
	on	Odd Parity *
2		not used
3		not used
4	off	DTR *
	on	BUSY
5	off	XON/XOFF enabled *
	on	Restraint enabled
6	off	Restraint normal *
	on	Restraint inverted

* means factory default setting


Hope it helps.

Marcus



