The HSC, like some other DEC hardware, use RT-11 file formats on
its media but doesn't really run RT-11.  There is the "year 2004"
issue if it date-stamps its files, but this may not matter if
the date-stamps don't count for anything.  Certainly the folks
inside DEC don't seem to be too worried about VMS Exchange
and the year 2004 issue, so maybe they've given up on such issues.
(Too bad if they have - it's so easy to fix!)

The one VAX-related piece of hardware that does run what I would
call a variant of "true" RT-11 is the VENUS (VAX 8600) console
subsystem, based around a PRO 380 running a derivative of
middling RT-11 V5.x.  RT-11 5.7 knows all about PRO's and
deals with the Y2K issues of the PRO's clock chip, but I
don't know if the VENUS console subsystem even cares about
this.

Tim.



