It means the HSC will continue to perform as expected. Don't take this as an
official statement, but as far as I know the HSCs will correctly transition
past 31st Dec 1999 and will correctly handle the Y2K leap year and will
correctly display dates in the 2000s. There may be cosmetic problems, but I
haven't heard of any. I believe that they will just keep on chugging.

An "OK" on that page should mean "no problems" except maybe cosmetic ones -
doesn't it say that somewhere?

As for the VAX consoles the only issues I am aware of are with the VAX 8600, 
VAX 85xx, VAX 8700 and VAX 88xx machines. There are some minor glitches with
their consoles (mostly cosmetic) but none of these will prevent the operation
of the associated VAX.

Note that I am not qualified to speak for anyone on Y2K issues (or pretty
much anything else) so take all the above with a suitable pinch of salt.

