> - Which was perhaps the use of this system ?

Who knows? Any of hundreds of things.

> - which was probably the OS (Unix version...) ?

Probably VMS, which is not Unix at all.

> - Was it a single user system ?

Almost certainly not. The async MUX (M3104) could connect 8 more terminals.

> - where can I get a "user handbook" for the muVAX (booting, meaning of the
>   front buttons of all components...) ?

If you didn't get one with the machine, chances are you'll never see one. Search
the net for more info.

> - Which type are the housings for this muVAX (BA23, BA123...) ?

This particular uvII is in paired BA23s, called a 630QE. Generally, it would
have two BA23s, connected to each other, with a RA8x drive below and something
else (perhaps another RA8x) above. Typically, it would also come with a TU8x
tape drive.

> - Why is this muVAX II SO BIG ??? (in comparision to the "under table

>   systems" which don't have TWO boxes for the cards...)

This system would have needed more storage - sort of a "computer room" model, as
opposed to a small office.

> - What is the difference between a Microvax II and a Vaxstation II ?

Graphics, and how many users are allowed. A VAXStation is a "Workstation", a
MicroVAX is a "Server".

> I have no Terminal to use as console
> - what kind of connector is the 9 pin SUBD connector on the backside
>   (bulkehead) ?

It's not quite RS232, but if you just grab the data pins, you'll be fine.

> - What kind of terminals can I connect ? (I have some SS97 Siemens Terminals
>   or a IBM colour Terminal...)

Sure, whatever you like. Should support at a minimum VT100.

> - Can I use a PC with a TTY or a VT100 emulation and a serial connector
>   cable ?

Yes and no - see my note about the serial cable above.

> - Do I have to use always a console to start the system (with a switch
>   on it or something like that) ?

Sometimes. If the battery backup has failed, you'll need to select a language
and boot device. Also, one of the switches on the back will prevent it from
automatically booting, forcing you to boot it from the console.

> Some of the cards are disassembled in the machine
> - Where in the muVAX processor housing 2) must I plug in the M 9404 card
>   coming from the "controller housing" 3) and which side must be on the
>   top ?

The components should go on "top" - just like all of the rest of the cards.
