> I am not firm with RA81 HDD
> - Where in the RA81 must I plug in the flat connector ?

Hmm... most RA81s came with the black strap permanently attached. Look on the
back, near the top.

> - Is only one of the four flat connectors for ONE RAxx drive ?

Each KDA50 supports 4 drives - pick a port, A or B. Just make sure that port is
available.

> - what are the two round mini 4 pin din connectors for in the RA81 ?

Power-up sequencing. In multi-drive situation, it makes sure that the drives
don't all try to spin up at the same time. Very bad for circuit breakers, that.

> - in which of the four flat connectors on the back of the system do I have
>   to plug in the RA81 ?

Any one. Perferably, the fist. (closest to top (left) of KDA50)

> - Is there any information about the SDI "standard" ?

I'm sure there is, but I don't have much. It was originially intended for
systems that would have many hds and have them far away from the controllers.
The SDI cable max is something like 200' - but MAKE SURE you always have an ODD
number of cables (including the red one internal), as the connectors do some
pair swapping.

> In both the processor and the controller housing are slots for connecting
> HDDs.
> - Do I need controllers for connecting drives there?

Yes. RQDX? controllers. It's MFM - but if you've got working SDI drives, I
wouldn't bother.

> - Is it MFM standard ?

Sort of. In fact, no.

> - When there are no drives in it, do the buttons on the front panel have
>   any function ?

Yes, but not the drive control buttons. The one button you'll use most is HALT -
it stops processing. Be wary of it...

> General...
> - How can I use the Ethernet connector (compatibility, wiring...) ?

Get a transciever. It's AUI, so unless you have a DELNI (like me) you'll need to
use a transciever to hook it into 10BaseT or 10Base2. Should be fairly cheap,
unless you want something that will out-perform the Vax.

> - What is the power supply for ? (one big INPUT, three OUTPUTS - all
>   220 V and 4 smaller outs !)

Extra drives, cabinets, what have you.

> - from which of the two harddisks (RA81, FUJITSU) does the system boot
>   from ?

Generally, which ever is connected to the first SDI strap. Unless you boot from
the console, in which case you can specify which one you want to boot from.

> - What are the 8 serial connectors for (Terminals...) ?

Yes. Or modems, serial printers, what have you.

> - For which use was the TK 50 tape for (booting, streamer...) ?

Backups, booting, what ever you might use a tape for.

> I also got a DEC VR262 screen together with the whole stuff, but I can't
> imagine that there is any use with the muVAX.
> - how can I use the VR262 ?

If you have the QDSS or QVSS, you could attach the VR262 to the uVII and have a
VSII/GPX.


I've got three uVII boardsets and one 3500 at home waiting for cases. If anyone
has any spares, please let me know. They would look really nice next to my two
3600s.
