In article <362F6CB9.61E8AC80@pao.mts.dec.com>,
Jean-Marie Verdun  <verdun@pao.mts.dec.com> wrote:
>800 Mhz EV6 has estimated performances which are: 55 SpecInt95  80 Specfp95 

This SPECint95 estimate is not very credible.  Given the value
of 30 on the 575 MHz AlphaServer 8400-6/575, I would say that 
41-42 is more likely.  SPECint95 scales linearly with clock
frequency within a given processor family once the L2 cache
is 1 MB or larger.

The SPECfp95 estimate is not out of the realm of possibility.  It
will, however, require a completely new system -- this level of
performance (80 SPECfp95) is not possible in a TurboLaser
(AlphaServer 8x00) system for any foreseeable cpu speed.  Assuming
Compaq sticks with a 4 MB L2 cache, simply upgrading the cpu speed
from 575 MHz to 800 MHz in the AlphaServer 8x00 will only increase
the SPECfp95 from its current value of 47.7 to about 58 (my estimate).

The AlphaServer 4100 line would make a slightly better starting 
point for an EV6 system, but we need to wait until Compaq announces
their next generation server before the SPECfp95 values begin to
approach the initial predictions.
-- 
