Lee K. Gleason <gleasonatmwk.com> writes:

>   I mean the firmware for the HSCs, that controls the thing..not really
> something I'm running...CRONIC they called it. It's RT-11 based,
> mostly...probably enough so to have the same date problems...and
> the HSCs know the date, they apparently get it from the VAXes in a
> cluster...the question is, will the RT variant stumble on the
> date problems, and will having a "funny" date in the HSCs affect
> cluster disk & tape operations?

RT-11 monitors run out of bits to store the year 2004, other parts of
it die at 2000.  Your controllers may do ok until 2004 but error logs
and such may quit at 2000.  If you can set the date ahead to test this
it's the easiest way to pin all it down (backup first just in case)...

You'd need at least V5.6 (or 5.7 depending on which utilities might be
in use here) to fix this, along with patching the HSC software - is DEC
still supporting this stuff?  5.6 was done in plenty of time to deal
with this but I don't know exactly what may have been done for HSCs.

Billy Y..



