Caroline,

I know this...

1. The Cirrus Logic GD542x is an old graphics chip.  As in really old.

2. If a driver is not on your OSF 4.0 installation media, you're
unlikely to find it.  

3. Do you have the liberty of installing another graphics card to
replace the graphics on the AS1000???  If so, check the OSF 4.0
documentation to see what graphics cards are directly supported.

4. Your AS1000, being older as well, may not comply with the PCI 2.1
specification, so an older card would have to do.

Let me know what you find out.  Maybe I can help with a graphics card
that is supported by OSF 4.0, which I don't have... Ben Myers 

