>billy@mix.com wrote:

> Jerome Fine <jhfine@idirect.com> writes:
> > Which utilities would you require at the minimum to even consider
> > using patches?
> I'd need everything working properly.  Monitors and all the utilities..

Jerome Fine replies:

Then I don't know why you were making an inquiry?  I specifically
stated that I wanted to help those commercial sites who are using
older versions of RT-11, and have specific reasons for remaining
with those older versions.   In addition, I felt that legal hobby users
might also wish, at a later date after Mentec has had an opportunity
to sell V5.7 to the hobby users (either the full H-kit with DOCS
at about $ US 1600  OR  the binary-only H-kit at a reduced price
if the user already has V5.6 of RT-11), to also consider V5.3 at a
very low price (perhaps around $ US 100) if Y2K was at all
important to hobby users who wished to use a legal version of
RT-11.

Mainly, I was trying to determine if there was any interest in Y2K
for older versions of RT-11 as well as to provide those commercial
users who are using V5.4G with the possibility of immediate patches
for some of the utilities if the stated utilities were all that it would be
useful to have.

If you absolutely must have everything working properly, not only the
Y2K aspects, but also all the other bugs that were in V5.6, then
definitely V5.7 is the most obvious way to go.  I only hope that
Mentec will at least honour the warranty on the software as opposed
to how DEC handled the situation.  The last time a customer
made a purchase from DEC many years ago of RT-11 software
and there were some bugs (fortunately before the payment was
made), DEC gave only 2 options:
(a) The software is sold as is (regardless of the warranty) and
      DEC does not correct bugs - indeed, would not even specify
      a price to correct the bug if the customer was willing to pay
(b) Send the software back.
Since you have such confidence in Mentec, I am sure you are
positive that Mentec will immediately correct any bugs in V5.7
free of charge and send the corrected files or programs to all
users as a free update.

> > And why do you want patches for V5.4G when
> > you are already using V5.6 of RT-11?
> I'm just curious about what this costs vs. what Mentec will be selling.
> I'll be using Mentec's release mainly because they were nice enough to
> actually buy it from DEC and make the effort to continue supporting it
> and I'm hoping whatever others do here won't be enough to make Mentec
> regret their decision..  As far as I know the release of V5.7, which
> is 100% Y2K compliant and supported by Mentec (a significant factor as
> well), is coming very soon now.

As long as V5.7 is supported by Mentec, that would be a big plus as
opposed to how DEC handled bugs.  But, when you say V5.7 is
supported by Mentec, does that mean that Mentec will charge for
another version when the bugs are fixed  AS  DEC used to do  OR
send free patches and programs that work to those users who buy
V5.7 of RT-11?  I would appreciate which way you define support:
(a)  Mentec charges to fix bugs in V5.7 regardless of whether it
      was DEC's fault or Mentec's fault, and does so only when
      there is enough profit to justify a release - perhaps never
(b) Mentec immediately sends out free patches and programs to fix
     the bugs in V5.7 of RT-11
(c) Some other definition which you are free to specify yourself.
     However, the prime aspect in any definition of support is how
     much the support for bug fixes will cost - and how fast they
     are done.  I don't consider any definition which omits either
     of these two aspects a definition which I can understand.

As a matter of my own opinion about V5.7, I agree very strongly
with most commercial users who have a reasonable budget to fix
the applications they are using if they also make a decision to
go with V5.7 of RT-11 as well.  In most cases, they cost of
any upgrade to V5.7 will likely be less than 10% of the total
cost of any project to make the complete system Y2K compliant.
So in principle, and in most cases, I agree with you and your
decision to purchase V5.7 of RT-11.

However, there are a few possible reasons for using only
patches for the current version of RT-11, whether it be
V5.6 or V5.4G or V5.3 or even V5.0 of RT-11 (or
maybe versions prior to V5.0 - very unlikely) such as:

(a) A limited amount of funds and only a few utilities
     are required for any version including current V5.6
     and all older versions
(b) A "NEED" to stay with the currently being used
      much less recent version, such as V5.4G, due to
      a requirement to reduce the QA needed to verify
      any newly released version such as V5.7 (I can
      offer a detailed example)
(c) Systems which run under TSX-PLUS already have
     a few conflicts with V5.6 and likely the same conflicts
     with V5.7 of RT-11.  In this case, the old version
     V5.4G (with Y2K patches for the utilities) might be
     the best place to stay.  They might also need a
     modified tape driver for TSX-PLUS which I could
     supply.
(d) Perhaps other readers can offer some examples

I have tried to discuss only current issues with regard to
how Mentec does or will support V5.7 of RT-11 and
stay away from decisions that took place many years
ago!  I did refer to what DEC used to do only to point
out an example of what I hope Mentec will not do when
Mentec is asked to fix the bugs in V5.7, as surely there
will be, even if they are leftovers from DEC.  I feel that
once Mentec actually releases V5.7, there is an obligation
to assume full responsibility for all RT-11 bugs.  Does
anyone else feel the same way?  Billy, do you feel that
way - that Mentec should immediately fix all bugs left
in V5.7 free of charge?

Sincerely yours,

Jerome Fine
Year 2000 Solutions for Currently Running RT-11 Operating Systems
and Applications  (Sources not always required)




