I have heard that there is a Multia model which only supports an
internal drive. Maybe you have such a beast. The 4 pin connector is
power. On Multias which support internal 3.5 inch and external drives,
the SCSI cable runs first to a disk drive connector, then to an external
SCSI-2 mini connector. It sounds like your version has a cable which
only goes to the internal drive.

In theory, you could make it work if you had the proper cable. However,
since it is soldered on to the riser card, that might be a bit tricky.
Getting a different riser card is the ideal solution, if the cards are
still available.

> 
> IS there a good source for half height PCI cards - or am I completely
> delusional in assuming the slot in the mother board is a pci slot?
> 

The slot in the motherboard may or may not be PCI, but it is only useful
for fitting the riser card (because of where the connectors on the card
would have to go). You can only fit a PCI card if you have the riser
card with a PCI slot. In this case, you have to use only 2.5 inch
internal drives or external drives.

What kind of PCI card would you like to use? I have a DE500 10/100
