In article <70eeap$98h$1@netra.msu.montana.edu>, tarka@msu.oscs.montana.edu (Mark Tarka) writes:
|>Anyone with hard facts on the outputs from the two power supplies
|>associated with a BA213 cabinet housing a uV3400?
|>

They both need to be working for the box as a whole to work. One supplied
power to the LH side of the backplane and the other does the other
half. IIRC the internal options (disks, tape) are split between them.

|>The box stops at "F" on the LED display of the CPU front panel if
|>the RH (right hand) PS (power supply) is used to power the installed
|>disk, but does an erratic "count-down" if the LH PS is used to
|>supply power to the disk.  The operator control panel (fixed disk
|>controls and indicators) does not show a green LED indicating DC OK. 
|>The fans no longer blow on start-up (did at an earlier time).

Each PSU needs enough load to actually come on (they are switched mode PSUs).
The one PSU will almost always be OK since it supplies power to the CPU, memory
and most other cards (since one generally fills the backplane from the memory
downwards). The other PSU may not have any load at all in which case you
should install a load-board (basically a quad card with a bunch of biggish
resistors and an LED or two - chances are you don't have one). Perhaps
this explains your problem. Alternatively you may have a flakey PSU or two.

Antonio

