Since you are posting in these news groups, I thought I might add a note
of practical use.  A friend of mine is using Oregon Pascal-2 RT-11 V2.1D
and naturally found that it is not Year 2000 compatible.  Does anyone
else also still use this compiler and either V2.1D or a version very close
to V2.1D?  While making other applications Year 2000 compatible,
the compiler itself (the listing header output) was made Year 2000
compatible.  The run-time routines that need to be made Year 2000
compatible have not been fixed as yet, but they are considered less
of a technical challenge since the OBJ is available.  If Oregon Software
is still around or the company or individual who now owns the Pascal-2
compiler wishes to claim priority, please do so.  Otherwise, if anyone
is still using the Pascal-2 RT-11 language, the patches for the compiler
for Year 2000 compatibility are available.

