The Philips 8X scsi CD-ROM drive appearently implements 512 mode
correctly because you are able to bootstrap and get to the $$$ of the
installation CD-ROM.

I am aware of a problem in the V7.1 SCSI driver with AlphaStation 255
systems and RZ26F disk.  This problem only occurs when the scsi is set
to fast mode.  As a workaround,

>>>set pka0_fast 0
>>>init

Hopefully, this will allow you installation to complete.

Install the following patch.
ftp://ftp.service.digital.com/public/vms/axp/v7.1/alpscsi01_071.README

Then, you may re-enable fast SCSI mode by
>>>set pka0_fast 1
>>>init
 
