connection, H4005 or DELNI, to connect to a Thickwire Ethernet
physical channel. The DECserver 700 supports both Thickwire and Twisted
Pair connections integral to the box.

<P>
<p>
<P>
<strong>OPTIONAL HARDWARE
</strong>
<P>
<p>
<P>
<strong>Terminals Supported
</strong>
<P>
The DECserver 700 software supports the following Digital Equipment
Corporation terminal devices that have keyboards:

<P>
<UL>
 <LI> LA12, LA34, LA35, LA36, LA38
 
<P>
<LI> All VTxxx terminals
 
<P>
</UL>
 Supported Terminal Parameters are:
 
<P>
<UL>
 <LI> Character size: 7- or 8-bits per character
 
<P>
<LI> Parity: Even, Odd, or None
 
<P>
</UL>
 The automatic line speed detection (Autobaud) feature is supported for
either 7-bit characters with even parity, or 8-bit characters with no
parity.
 
<P>
The DECserver 700 software also supports DIGITAL Asian terminal device 
variants when accessed from VMS/Hanzi systems.

<P>
The DECserver 700 software also supports DIGITAL Asian terminal device 
variants when accessed from VMS/Japanese systems.

<P>
The DECserver 700 software also supports the following DIGITAL Personal 
Computers (PCs) in both terminal emulation mode and file transfer 
mode:

<P>
<UL>
 <LI> VAXmate
 
<P>
<LI> DECstation
 
<P>
</UL>
 Note: This product will also operate on non-DIGITAL terminal devices
or personal computers such as terminals supporting VT100- or VT200-like 
characteristics, and personal computers supporting IBM[R] PC, IBM
PC/XT, and IBM PC/AT[R] characteristics may operate with this product.
 
<P>
<p>
<P>
<strong>Printers Supported
</strong>
<P>
The DECserver 700 software supports the following DIGITAL asynchronous
printers when accessed from VMS systems:

<P>
<UL>
 <LI> All LJ, LA, LQP, LXY, LN0, LG, and DTC printing devices.
 
<P>
</UL>
 The DECserver 700 software also supports DIGITAL Asian printer device
variants when accessed from VMS/Hanzi systems.
 
<P>
The DECserver 700 software also supports DIGITAL Asian printer device
variants when accessed from VMS/Japanese systems.

<P>
<p>
<P>
<strong>Modems Supported
</strong>
<P>
Both DECserver 700 models support asynchronous devices with interfaces
that conform to EIA/TTA-232-E/CCITT V.24/V.28.

<P>
Additionally, DECserver 700 models support DIGITAL modems including
DF03, DF112, DF124, DF224, DF242, DFM X.29 pad, and DECmodem V32 fullduplex 
asynchronous modems for either dial-in or dial-out applications.
However, connections to data switches are NOT WARRANTED but may operate 
with this product.

