And... (c) Initially, it was sold with virtually no useful software for
the average home user. (A year or so later, there was a version of WPS
for it.)  (d) Initially, there were no software development tools 
available that ran directly on it. (All those kids in high school and
college who would have given their eye teeth to learn to program a
PDP11, and no software development tools.).  Just another example in the
chain of DEC's shooting itself in the foot, then the legs, then the
stomach, then the chest, and, finally, right between the eyes.

