I am running OVMS 6.2 on an Alpha Server 2100A with a RAID 200
controller.  I now have six 2.1GB drives arranged as two JBODs and
one 4 disk RAID 5 logical drive.  Each of the logical drives is in
its own group.

I have new drives that I want to replace some of the old drives with.
I want to replace one JBOD drive (system disk) with two 4GB drives
in a RAID 1 configuration. The second JBOD (utility disk) will be
combined with the old system disk in a RAID 1 configuration.
I will replace the four 2.1GB disks with three 9GB disks in a RAID 5
configuration.

The first move will be to put the 4GB drives in  the two open slots that
I now have as a new RAID 1 set in a new group and move the
operating system to it.  I will run that way for a while.  I will then make
the RAID 1 set for the utility disk.  Then later I will replace the
RAID 5 disks.

My question is, when I get around to reorganizing the drives, can I do
so without reinitializing and restoring backups or can I move drives
around in the SCSI slots and assign them to new groups and logical RAID
drives without losing the data?  I was hoping that preserving the order of
the physical drives in the logical set would keep the data usable.

Of course, the RAID 5 replacement  will require a restore but if
something goes wrong I would like to quickly reconfigure and plug in
the four old 2.1GB disks and go.

Don Marchlenski




