I'm selling my DECstation 5000/240 UNIX workstation.

It is running Ultrix 4.3, and comes with the Ultrix CD.
The system also runs NetBSD and OpenBSD.
- http://www.netbsd.org/Ports/pmax/index.html
- http://www.openbsd.org/pmax.html

Here are some system specs on the system...
- 40 Mhz RISC (MIPS, aka pmax) processor
- 64k internal cache, 64k external cache
- 128 MB System RAM
- around 700 MB disk space, not certain...
  There are 3 SCSI hard drives, of which I am only using one (540MB)
  The other two are an apple 80MB and a maxtor 170MB (I think)
- Two DEC SCSI Storage Expansion boxes (housing the hard drives)
  Each holds 2 drives.  You could probably cram more than two in each 
  box, but there's only mounting brackets and ribbon cable plugs for 
  two drives per box.
- Built-in LANCE ethernet (10Mbps)
- Fast PMAGB-BA Graphics Card (1280x1024 @ 66 Hz or 72 Hz)
- External SCSI CD-ROM (Probably only 1x) and caddy
- Keyboard and mouse (The good kind, not the terrible hockey puck)
- "Guide to installing ULTRIX" manual.  This might come in handy if 
  you ever need to re-install the OS.
- Includes all the cables you need...
  3 SCSI cables, SCSI Terminator
  4 Power cables
  Keyboard/Mouse bus cable
  2 Extra long monitor cables

I have the system set up so that you can verify that it works before 
you buy.

Price... $300 OBO.  With a heavy emphasis on the "or best offer."
  I will lower the price to $250 OBO if I keep the cdrom, one scsi 
  cable, and one power cable.  You'd still get the Ultrix CD and 
  a cd caddy.

Please email rive@mail.utexas.edu, or call 512-478-3701 if 
interested.  I really don't want to ship this.  I will ship it, but 
Austin, TX area buyers will be preferred.

THE SYSTEM DOES NOT INCLUDE A MONITOR.
I have a monitor here for testing purposes, but it is not for sale.
Supposedly, NetBSD and OpenBSD can use a VT Terminal in place of a 
monitor.  I have never tried this, and I cannot tell you how to do 
it.  You'll probably want to buy a monitor for the system.  There 
is probably a way to make a standard multi-sync monitor work with 
the DECstation, but you would have to be one smart cookie to figure 
that one out.  The system drives a sync-on-green fixed-frequency 
monitor at 1280x1024x8bpp @ 66 Hz or 72 Hz.  You'll want a monitor 
that will sync on 66 and/or 72 Hz.  Any Sony GDM-1961 should work, 
including the DEC VRT-19HA, several HP models, and maybe more.  If 
you shop around, you should be able to find such a monitor for 
between $50 and $150 or so.  Most sell for $75.  You can pay more, 
but you shouldn't have to if you shop around.  To start you out, 
search for 'fixed frequency' and 'fixed-sync' in the "for sale" 
section on www.dejanews.com.  Or, perhaps you already have such a 
monitor.  That would really be a plus.  I don't know if XYZ monitor 
will work, so please don't send me email asking me.  :)



