X.\" This manpage source uses rsml coding. 
X.so /usr/share/lib/tmac/sml
X.so /usr/share/lib/tmac/rsml
X.TH ldd 1 "" "" "" "local" ""
X.SH NAME
X.PP
\*Lldd\*O \- List dynamic dependencies.
X.SH SYNOPSIS 
X.PP 
X.sS
\*Lldd\*O
\*Vfile\*O
\&.\&.\&.
X.sE 
X.PP
ldd attempts to list the dynamically loaded objects on which \*Vfile\*O depends.
X.PP
X.SH FLAGS
X.PP 
None
X.SH DESCRIPTION
X.PP 
X.iX "ldd command"
X.iX "list dynamic" "dependencies"
X.iX "shared" "libraries"
For each of the files given as arguments, ldd tries to expand the
dynamically loaded files that it needs to run, and resolve them to file names of
shared objects on the system. It searches for the shared objects using the
same algorithm as documented in the manual page for \*Lloader\*O(1) (but see
BUGS, below.)
X.RE 
X.SH DIAGNOSTICS
X.PP
\*Lldd\*O can output the following error messages:
X.VL 4m
X.LI "\*Vfile\*O is not a regular, readable file, ignored"
\*Lldd\*O was unable to open the file.
X.LI "\*Ocouldnt ldopen \*Vfile\*O, not an executable?"
\*Lldd\*O does not think the file is an OSF/1 executable.
X.LI "\*Vfile\*O not dynamically linked"
\*Lldd\*O does not think the file is dynamically linked. Perhaps it is statically
linked?
X.LE
X.SH RELATED INFORMATION
X.PP 
\*Lloader\*O(1), \*Lld\*O(1), \*Lldfcn\*O(4) (yeah, right, \*Lldfcn\*O(4) - how about
updating it, DEC?)
X.SH BUGS
X.PP
Probably. Its not been extensively leaned on. If you find a bug, let
me know, and I'll look at fixing it. Most of the assumptions were from
DEC's man pages, so there are probably erroneous ones in there.
X.PP
It could do with better error messages. It doesnt (yet) handle _RLD_ROOT
or _RLD_LIST environment variables.
X.SH AUTHOR
X.PP
Anthony Baxter, <anthony@aaii.oz.au>
X.PP
