The reason Compaq doesn't recommend/sell the Polycenter suite as part of BRS
is that they were not aware that you could purchase the point products
separately.  Ca's announcement during Decus caught the product manager
totally by surprise.  It's sure a good thing that they're such good
partners!

Whether or not BRS will migrate back to ConsoleIT and WatchIT will be
interesting to watch.  Personally, I found Watchdog pretty weak, and have
replaced it with Robomon.  I'll likely be using PCM/ConsoleIT myself, since
we've already got the license.

The license upgrade from CA was actually fairly reasonably priced, if you
needed a lot more licenses than you had originally purchased from Digital.
The new licenses are all 0 unit VMS licenses, with no expiration date, and
you can put them on as many VMS systems as you want.  The only system that
CA cares about is the TNG server that runs on the NT system.  For those of
us that prefer managing systems from VMS, unlimited licensing is a good
thing!

