skrass@my-dejanews.com writes:
> Hi, Is there a trick to using a non-DEC cdrom on a vaxstation? I am trying
> to load VAX VMS 7.1 from cdrom on to a blank hard disk.  The cdrom is a
> Philips 8X scsi.  The vax recognizes the cdrom drive correctly and will even
> boot the 'X6NO Major Version' to a "$" prompt but as soon as I type a backup
> command I get: "DKA400: is offline.  Mount verification in progress"  The
> light on the cdrom drive comes on and the system never comes back.

  You want a CDROM drive that can be permanently set to use a 512 byte sector
size instead of the normal 2048 bytes. Many drives accept a MODE SELECT com-
mand to set the sector size, but I don't know of any CDROM drives with non-
volatile mode pages.

  Aside from the obvious DEC drives, Sun drives also come set for 512 byte
operation. The Plextor brand drives have a jumper or DIP switch to set this
mode. Some other drives have undocumented jumpers or firmware mods - see
http://saturn.tlug.org/suncdfaq/suncds.htm (only drives listed there that can
be put into a permanent 512 byte/sector mode will work).

  Personally, I just use the Plextor UltraPlex drives - the list price for
the internal tray version is $189 and they guarantee VMS compatibility.

