> does anybody know how to get a *8 inch floppy onto a 3 1/2 floppy

You'll have to be more specific about what originally wrote the 8"
floppy, and what operating system was running on it.  But
since you're posting to "comp.sys.dec", I'll assume that it's
a RX01 or RX02 floppy written by RT-11, RSX-11, or VMS, in which
case all you need is an appropriate computer system with both
8" and 3.5" drives.  For example, a VAX with attached RX02 drive
clustered with a workstation with a 3.5" floppy would be able to
read any of the RT-11, RSX-11, or VMS file formats from 8" floppy
and put the files on 3.5" floppy.

I (and others) provide commercial media transfer services which are
capable of doing the above task with a turnaround time measured in
minutes.

