In article <3619A307.214B@ns.sympatico.ca>, Catherine Vey <vey.cathy@ns.sympatico.ca> writes:
>I am planning on upgrading from DECnet Phase IV to DECnet OSI in order
>to be Y2K compliant and to get X.25 access on a VAX/VMS system.
>
>Can anyone tell me if X.25 access is provided to a VAX/VMS system
>through DECnet/OSI?  The info I have implies it is only for an Alpha.

PSI and PSIaccess (the old names of the X25 software running with DN4)
and the WAN-Drivers are an integral part of DECnet-Plus (formerly
DECnet/OSI) on OpenVMS VAX only.

On OpenVMS Alpha there is an addional product X.25.

The good news:
A PSIaccess License is not required with DECnet-Plus on OpenVMS VAX.

The bad news:
PSIaccess functionality (GAP Gateway Access Protocol) is provided only
from a DECnis router - which is almost dead now - or from other long dead
Digital router products.

My advise is, consider leaving X.25 or better not getting it.
If you must, think of big bucks for the X.25 licenses and a LLC2 capable
router (eg. X25 Relay in a CISCO)

just my 0.02
