>
>8. Are DecStation3100s the same as VaxStation3100s?  I have seen
>mostly VaxStation references around the usenet!

Most certainly not!
They appear int he same enclosure (BA42) and have similar interfaces, 
but are quite different machines. 
The VS3100 is a VAX machine with a CVAX processor . 
The DS3100 is a RISC box with a MIPS R2000A processor. 
The architecture of the machines' devices are similar: they use the same
serial interface subsystem, same ethernet hardware, same SCSI adaptor (though
the VAxstation has two SCSI buses) , and nearly the same video hardware, 
but internally they are quite different. 

happy hacking,
gregg




