I mean that controlling GUI elements via a script does not feel natural.
For purely CLI-based applications CLI-based scripts feel minimalistic
and logical - a strong concept originally behind UNIX. You have the same
file-based input/output that applies to everything. I'm not suggesting
there is any better method to control GUI applications (GUIs tend to raise
the level of complexity quite considerably), just that CLI scripters in 
a sense have a much clearer view of life than their GUI brothers.

