The NiCad battery packs that I've seen for the MicroVAXs have 3 cells. 
A NiCad battery should have a cell voltage of about 1.2 to 1.3 volts 
per cell.  You should be able to come up with the battery pack voltage 
by taking 1.2 or 1.3 and multiplying by the number of cells.  For  
other types of batteries in other systems, but you should be able to 
follow a similar method.

