>What is the external SCSI connector on the back of a VAXstation 3100
>called?  Is it useful for conventional external SCSI devices (e.g.
>a ZIP disk or CD-ROM reader)?  Where can I get the appropriate
>adaptor/cable?  Is there a DEC part number for this?

Terence,
     this is, by my understanding, another example of DEC following an 
emerging standard and having that standard modified out from under the,.
Its a 68-pin male clip-type connector, requiring a cable with a female
socket end; I have no idea if anyone else makes them, but the DEC part
nymber I have for such a beast is BC56H-03; this has a standard SCSI-1
Centronics 50 at the other end.

     My VAXstation 3100/76's and the 3100-30 at work have the same 
connector; using this cable I have attached external DEC and Quantum
disks, tapes, and a Pioneer 32X SCSI CDrom with good results.

     The cables are moderately common; for a long time DEC would ship
one of these along with a standard centronics-centronics with peripherals
sold for 3100 systems.  Don't know if they are still orderable...

Rich Jordan
rjordan@mcs.net




