>root/supervisor without having to know the passwords ??


OK, depending on your knowledge of VMS, several pages may be of interest.

First of all the VMS FAQ at ftp://ftp.digital.com/pub/Digital/dec-faq/vms
specifically:-
MGMT5.  I've forgotten the SYSTEM password - what can I do?

Should solve your password problem.

Note that this ONLY works from the CONSOLE port.
If  you don't know which is the console port on a MVII, you should really
have a look at the Microvax/Vaxstation FAQ at
http://anacin.nsc.vcu.edu/~jim/mvax/mvax_faq_text.html
Specifically:-
4f) What's what on the back panel, or bulkhead, of a MicroVAX II?
Pay particular attention to the pinout of the 9 pin console connector, which
is somewhat different to (current) standards.
The VMS FAQ has some more specific info on this, IMHO, you really need to
look at both documents.

Hope this helps.  Have fun with it, I have my very own MVII with VMS 5.4 on
it, plus a small herd of
Vaxstations. (Plus a Vax 6220 I play with at work :^)

