John Stephen Haro wrote:
> 
> Hello,
> 
> We have been tasked to gather monthly usage metrics automatically for
> our 50+ DEC AlphaNT workstations. This is to provide data primarily for
> assest allocation purposes.
> 
> [Q] Can anyone recommend a method or third party software that is simple
> to use, and/or not cost much per client seat? The basic info we would be
> interested in gathering would be, 1)logon time, 2)processor utilization,
> 3)network I/O per seat, that we could plot in charts for upper
> management.
> --
> Thanks,
> pls. email back or call me, I don't read news that often.
> John S. Haro
> Boeing Defense and Space Group, Seattle, WA
> john.s.haro@boeing.com (206)655-1775

BCAG Engineering developed a suite of UNIX utilization reports under the
name "USEM" (UNIX System Efficiency Metrics).

Now, I know this is of little use on NT, but you might learn from our
experience. I was on the team that developed USEM, and we could not
define "utilization" to everyone's satisfaction (thus the name
"Efficiency"). There's no single number that shows machine X is "under
utilized" and thus can be surplussed (which is what managers wanted). I
even submitted an ARR (Architecture Review Request) asking BCAG IS to
define utilization so we could develop tools to generate common
utilization numbers across platforms, but the ARR was rejected -- the
potato was just too hot.

Good luck with your search, but prepare to defend machines that don't
measure up. For your sake, I hope you don't find what you're looking
for!
-- 
Rick Downer
BCAG I/S, Renton
richard.k.downer@boeing.com



