In article <361A4AEE.3231@boeing.com>, john.s.haro@boeing.com wrote:
>Hello,
>
>We have been tasked to gather monthly usage metrics automatically for
>our 50+ DEC AlphaNT workstations. This is to provide data primarily for
>assest allocation purposes.
>
>[Q] Can anyone recommend a method or third party software that is simple
>to use, and/or not cost much per client seat? The basic info we would be
>interested in gathering would be, 1)logon time, 2)processor utilization,
>3)network I/O per seat, that we could plot in charts for upper
>management.

The PerfMon program that comes with NT will provide most of the information 
you need.  It can be used remotely and has a logging only option that will 
have less impact on the remote machine.  The logon usage can be done by 
auditing logons to the event viewer log.  Again this can be accessed remotely.

If you want an in depth tutorial on how to use PerfMon pick up a copy of the 
NT 4 Workstation resource kit.  There are several hundred pages on how to use 
PerfMon to find peformance bottlenecks.

Paul



