Some DS3100 have problems booting via tftp/bootp, especially the KN01 7.0
firmware versions. Booting via MOP works in most cases and there
is a working mopd for Linux and *BSD. I only used it to upgrade the firmware
of my 3000/300X Alpha so far ... more information on booting DECstations
via tftp can be found on the DECstation Linux www site.

[...]
:> 5. What is the >likely< specification of the two DS3100's? ie. in
:> terms of memory, hdd's, etc.

Maximum 24 MB RAM, hard disk could be anything from a RD23 (ca. 100 MB) to a
RZ26 (1 GB). The DECstation 2100/3100 either had a monochrome (1024x864 b/w)
or color frame buffer (1024x864, 8 bit color depth) frame buffer depending
on the video RAM SIMM installed.

:> 6. Could I use a CDROM (scsi) from a Sun Sparc LX on the DS3100's as a
:> boot medium?

: 	Don't know on this one either.

Might work. The CDROM from the LX should already be set to deliver 512 byte
sectors (instead of the 2 kB sectors that CD-ROMs usually have), so you
might be lucky. I bought a used DEC RRD42 (Toshiba XM4101 CD-ROM with
DEC-specific firmware) just to be sure ... 

