David Gray wrote:

> Hi,
>
> Is it possible to let the authorize function assign unique UIC
> values when creating a new account in authorize?
>

The autorize function itself won't do this but you can write somecode to
wrap around authorize to accomplish it. I have seen several
different versions.

> In the past I have added new users by copying from another account
> then changing the UIC to a new value.  Are there any drawbacks with
> letting the accounts all have the default [200,200] value?
>

Well, it depends on the application. My current users all login to
onedirectory and all the application files are g:rwed and in this case
it
is not too much of a problem having many users assigned the same uic
(the previous admins actually set up most account like that). However,
if you want to have per user file security and accountability then you
need
a unique UIC per username. Get used to UAF > copy/uic. Personally
I don't like setting up accounts with the same UIC, its lazy and bad
practice
if nothing else.

> Thanks in advance.
>
> David.



--
