Sun decided for a number of reasons to write Solaris from
scratch.
One big factor was the difficulty in re-structuring SunOS
and building 
new services and functions into the OS. The first Solaris
2.x itterations 
were not more reliable than SunOS but because the OS had
been re-architected 
it was possible to fix those issues.

SunOS was allong with many OS's of that era a big wad of
code
you changed something in one part of the OS and something 
