We have a number of Alpha servers, and although we use a bigger DLT for 
RAID backups we have always used the TLZ09 series 4mm for regular backups, 
and incrementals.  THey work well with DEC stuff because DEC has built in 
support for that drive in most running kernels.  Be careful though on some 
older model Alphas like the DEC 2000/500 crashed big time when we tried 
bumping up the compression. The New 4100, and the 2100 's work well with 
it.  I don't know about the 8?00 series machines though.




