I think the vastly is streaching it a bit. VMS backup may have alot
more to do in getting certain file types to and from tape/disk
but it hardly does anything more for the user interface and function
than it ever did! Its taken a long time for VMS to have file status
to indicate if the file is Shelved/online (ie. HSM) And you still
have to get more to make it work. TOPS-20 had this years before.
Feature by Feature VMS should be so much further a head from TOPS
but its not, its alive and well still which is more than I can say
for TOPS but thats DEC's choice in VMS not the fault of the OS's
VMS was build out of PDP11/RSX11M -> VAX/VMS
PDP11 with Virtual Address eXtention
RSX   with Virtual Memory System

I think its distance from its roots can be measured more by the years
than the features. Though I've always liked VMS though there are some 
things not to like and it could be better, its stable enough and 
nobody I've seen completes the cluster story so well.


