	No I think ignorance is now MacOS's "most serious defficiencies"
MacOS has had scripting now for some time, just because you don't know 
about it doesn't mean it doesn't exist.
The finder and most application are scriptable
eg.
tell application "Finder"
 repeat with w in every container window
  try -- this will skip over non-list view windows
  set calculates folder sizes of w to (not calculates folder sizes of w)
  on error
  end try
 
 end repeat
end tell

This is just from the examples. The language is based on that used
by hypercard and later by MacroMedia Director.  Its simple
and event driven. It can and is used to glue applications together ,
you can even front end things with dialogs and input boxes and pull
information from one application do some internal work on it and stuff
it through several other applications to get a result. Not everything 
is scriptable though its getting better.


